{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/822963-best-set-of-house-rules","id":822963,"title":"Best set of House Rules?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-02-03T19:11:41-08:00","id":822963,"title":"Best set of House Rules?","content":"I'm new to Scion, and though I know it has a lot of blemishes on it, it is still rather charming to me. I came to ask what you guys would reccommend to be a good set of House Rules that fix most of the problems in the game. The one major thing I'm aware of is Dex as a god stat, but that's it. I have the JSR Compendium which has a list of house rules, but I'm not sure how great they are.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11157-smarttman","name":"smarttman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-03T20:33:30-08:00","id":823018,"title":"","content":"There are a few sets of house rules that are pretty well known. They all tend to fiddle with the system to different degrees and sometimes introduce new concepts. I believe all of these have changes made to the Associated Powers and Abilities of Divine Parents as well as what I'll list.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://www.thecbg.org/wiki/index.php?title=Modern_Mythos\" target=\"_blank\">Modern Mythos</a> is a set of house rules written by Brentnotbroken here on the forums. It's got a host of Knacks, Boons, and little fixes. It's probably the closest to RAW.<br /> <br /> Telgar also has a set of <a href=\"http://www.thecbg.org/wiki/index.php?title=House_Rules_%28Lost_Atlanta%29\" target=\"_blank\">house rules</a> for his games as well, they are quite in depth focused with several larger changes such as introducing Ultimate Abilities, but keeping the system familiar to core.<br /> <br /> JSR/GBN's house rules are written by John and Anne, who have now moved on to doing some of their own game writing. Their system is more divergent from RAW, but their added Pantheons are written in a style which allows them to be slotted into RAW very neatly without much difficulty. Their rules are really neat, and should be pretty familiar to anyone who has played RAW before. The only <i>really</i> tricky part of their system is their Fate System which is a bit arcane. It's a brilliant set of rules though.<br /> <br /> Then there is <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/scionoverhaul/home\" target=\"_blank\">Scion 2.0</a> which is still being expanded upon. It's expansive and has taken a hatchet to a lot of the existing rules for various reasons. It is probably the most alien when compared to RAW. I'm one of the three people who work on it, so, I'm obviously biased towards it which I'd want to point out.<br /> <br /> But, you're totally correct with RAW having Dex as a god-tier Stat. If you want to use RAW, one of the biggest changes to make it at least try to look a bit balanced is change Untouchable Opponent to add Dots of Epic Dex, not Successes to Dodge DV.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Scion 2e Homebrew Projects:<br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1BUnAIZEDk4Zs_W0ELfffeFRAiSel3nAl/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The \u0160iune\u0161</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1MMw0vBmHdvuGUbVhyFw7BpXT49UgECnR/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Enduri</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1CZuVp5VuftwuwHtzrWADqIaq7Vl-LMIr/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Sg\u0101\u2019na Qeda\u2019s</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/17piJ8ZBzvt4PL47vz5Gw3BF6HOZelrfh/view?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">The Abosom</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/282712/Lebor-Oe-In-Dea?src=newest_community\" target=\"_blank\">Lebor \u00d3e In Dea</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1rk9BKLqbUEroFDvuPSQOwp-pBRxSvN9P/view\" target=\"_blank\">The Zemi</a>, <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/324026/Nemetondevos-Revised\" target=\"_blank\">Nemetondevos: Revised</a>, and <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/325461/Mysteries-of-the-Otherworld\" target=\"_blank\">Mysteries of the Otherworld</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/394-watcher","name":"Watcher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"662"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T04:53:43-08:00","id":823230,"title":"","content":"JSR had the best website and was really good. Just stay away from their Fate rules. They also have lots of great pantheon PDFs, and ran an awesome blog.<br /> <br /> Scion 2,0 is the second best thing around. More balanced than JSR. They are outright missing some purviews though, and updates are really slow.<br /> <br /> There are a couple of other websites where you can nab good knacks and boons, like Mosh Pits, Modern Mythos, and Atlanta. But JSR and Scion 2,0 are the big ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2447-twitchtherat","name":"TwitchTheRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2447_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T06:07:33-08:00","id":823269,"title":"","content":"I actually was asking about how to house rule the Dex thing a while ago too. Got some advice that maybe you scale down the automatic successes to 1 per rank. That way, at most you get 10 auto successes, instead of 40, plus extra die rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-04T15:16:00-08:00","id":823765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>smarttman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/822963-best-set-of-house-rules#post822963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm new to Scion, and though I know it has a lot of blemishes on it, it is still rather charming to me. I came to ask what you guys would reccommend to be a good set of House Rules that fix most of the problems in the game. The one major thing I'm aware of is Dex as a god stat, but that's it. I have the JSR Compendium which has a list of house rules, but I'm not sure how great they are.<br /> <br /> Thanks for any help!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here is the best set of Houserules till 2nd ed comes out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine?term=chuubo\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/images/4195/134196.jpg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine?term=chuubo\" target=\"_blank\"> Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine - Jenna Katerin Moran | DriveThruRPG.com </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine?term=chuubo\" target=\"_blank\"> http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/134196/Chuubos-Marvelous-WishGranting-Engine?term=chuubo </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Chuubo's Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine - The Chuubo&rsquo;s Marvelous Wish-Granting Engine RPG is the new diceless RPG from Jenna Katerin Moran, author of the well-r </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T12:25:46-08:00","id":824517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/822963-best-set-of-house-rules?p=823269#post823269\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I actually was asking about how to house rule the Dex thing a while ago too. Got some advice that maybe you scale down the automatic successes to 1 per rank. That way, at most you get 10 auto successes, instead of 40, plus extra die rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'm not sure that nerfing one attribute is fair to those people that have that as a core concept. There are plenty of ways to deal with a dex monkey (area attacks, animal aspect, many on one attacks from minions). I think the 'problem' of dex can be resolved by allowing other knacks/powers that will balance things out. For example a strength knack that allows you to use your strength/epic strength to hit instead of Dex. It's already in the core rules for Grappling, allowing it for unarmed/melee combat isn't that much of a stretch and allows the majority of big brusers and war gods (Thor, Ares, Herc, Huitzilopochtli, Anhur, Set, Bia, Kratos, Tyr) to remain viable concepts in a fight instead of getting their asses handed to them consistantly if you rolled dice instead of just describing a fight between them. <br /> <br /> Same thing for those war gods that are more strategists (Athena comes to mind as someone that consitantly defeated Ares in battle but has no epic physicals). Make a war Boon that while active allows them to substitute their Int or Wits for Dex to put them on even footing by visualizing/planning the fight in their head and making it happen or whatever it is that their mind does to allow them to win battles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/333-achilles","name":"Achilles","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar333_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-05T14:16:02-08:00","id":824579,"title":"","content":"I meant you should nerf all the attributes, because 40 automatic successes +40 dice rolls +Knacks seems a tad extreme for combat. Outside of combat, we discussed leaving them at full power for the purpose of stunts or plot related activities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T06:47:43-08:00","id":824918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/822963-best-set-of-house-rules?p=824579#post824579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant you should nerf all the attributes, because 40 automatic successes +40 dice rolls +Knacks seems a tad extreme for combat. Outside of combat, we discussed leaving them at full power for the purpose of stunts or plot related activities.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would leave you very weak to mortals, unless that is the kind of game you are trying to run. I think I saw Telgar mention a while back that he was running a game with a house rule like that. Maybe he could share his experiences? I think he is one of the few old posters still around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-02-06T14:20:24-08:00","id":825093,"title":"","content":"I was in at least one of Telgar's &quot;lower powered&quot; games. I think the one in question. Focusing in on trying to make things work in one regard did create some balance where there wasn't much before, but it also highlighted some other areas where Scion is weak, such as, Boons become a much more desirable when attributes aren't WMDs. And Boons are actually more than a little thin on the ground, more than a bit inconsistent from Purview to Purview and mechanically something of a mess. <br /> <br /> Partially due to some of these issues and partly due to the group just not having much in the way of a common purpose (to the level of some characters's plans being outright at odds with each other), it all fell apart right after the transition to Demigod.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}